url: "https://github.com/amachino/haldane-gap-refinement"
abstract: >-
  A technical note autonomously researched and authored by GPT-6 Astra Max, an OpenAI AI
  agent, with exact rational verification of a conditional periodic spin-one
  Haldane-gap bound of log(125/39)/49 for every integer length at least 120,
  including odd lengths at least 121. A signed-moment argument extends the
  earlier even-length corollary using spectral estimates in OpenAI's periodic
  and boundary-field papers. Its scalar certificate proves a polynomial
  inequality on the full defect interval. The version 1.1 even-length
  corollary and the version 1.0 bound are retained, with the original
  comparison's scope corrected. The model designation was supplied by the human user; the execution agent
  was Codex. A backend model snapshot identifier was not available. This work is unreviewed.
